          %h2#summary Summary
          %p
            The
            %em Tietze extension theorem
            says that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extend
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subsets"} closed subsets
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+topological+space"} normal topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the whole space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This is a close cousin of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urysohn%27s+lemma"} Urysohn's lemma
            with many applications.
          %p
            One implication is that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
            over a topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            that trivialize over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspace"} closed subspace
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            are equivalent to vector bundles on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/A
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "topological+vector+bundle#OverClosedSubspaces"} there
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+in+cohomology"} long exact sequence in cohomology
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "topological+K-theory#ExactSequences"} there
